{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1254301-ex-2-5-the-shaft-given-to-solars-and-lunars-when-facing-superior-magnitudes","id":1254301,"title":"[EX 2.5] The shaft given to Solars and Lunars when facing superior magnitudes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-14T12:38:16-07:00","id":1254301,"title":"[EX 2.5] The shaft given to Solars and Lunars when facing superior magnitudes","content":"Posting cause my friends like 2.5 and don't want to move onto 3e yet. And so something I discovered when creating a Dawn general.<br /> <br /> So... out of the celestial exalted charms in 2,5 that give bonuses fighting large numbers of forces alone, it seems Solars get the short end of the stick.<br /> <br /> Infernals have Opened Eye of the Hurricane, an essence 3 charm which negates magnitude bonuses for units fighting the Infernal.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals get the essence 3 charm Hundredfold Strafing Methodology, which negates dv bonuses for superior magnitude and doubles or triples attack roll success when fighting against magnitude 3+ unit. <br /> <br /> Abyssals get Glorious Carnage Typhoon at essence 3, which acts similar to the Hundredfold Strafing Methodology for magnitude and attack successes. No mirror.<br /> <br /> But the Solars, they don't get their charm when facing superior magnitudes until essence 6. In Doubt of Legions Spirit. And that only inflicts a penalty against the unit for the difference in magnitude subtracted by might. <br /> <br /> So... what gives? Why do Solars have to wait until essence 6 to do about roughly half of what the essence 3 charms for Alchemicals and Abyssals can do?<br /> <br /> Lunars of course are shafted as well. They can ignore magnitude bonuses when targeting specific individuals when fighting as a solo unit only. You think they'd be going and going berserk and shattering armed units trying to strike at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T12:51:57-07:00","id":1254305,"title":"","content":"Because 2e (and 2.5e) was a constant struggle between the writing forces of 'Solars are the best at everything no one gets to beat them. Period&quot; and &quot;The Usurpation killed all the Solars and the entire setting doesn't work if this is not true&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T07:37:45-07:00","id":1254507,"title":"","content":"The biggest &quot;why&quot; is that 2e lacked coherent mechanical development until pretty late in the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T15:24:18-07:00","id":1254635,"title":"","content":"Hmm... As I remember it, GCT was an Abyssals 1e Charm that lacked a Solar equivalent, and again if I recall correctly, this was a stylistic choice, where the idea was the image of a sole guy with a sword killing mass swathes of soldiers better fit the violent, bloodied, brutal, lonely thematics of Abyssals than the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> (And I can kind of admit I actually have a sympathetic bias towards this; it seems like heroes should find a better way to break an enemy army than just killing everyone as a sole guy, and if you can't, then it against seems more Solar to be the haughty shining lord dropping mass death through some sorcery or a powerful evocation. Solars are not typically, in my mind's eye, grinning maniacs, razor in hand, standing on a mountain of corpses.)<br /> <br /> 2e mostly ran where possible on upgrading 1e sets so that games could continue seamlessly from one edition to another, and so when the time comes to upgrade the Abyssals set, GCT became integrated into the mass combat.<br /> <br /> I assume the story for the Alchie Charm is pretty similar (initially a mass fighting Charm deemed to &quot;fit&quot; with Alchies, then upgraded for 2e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}